<title>HUNGARY: Hungary boosts housing construction in 1996 - KSH.</title>
<headline>Hungary boosts housing construction in 1996 - KSH.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarians finished the construction of 28,257 flats in 1996, compared with only 24,718 in 1995 and 20,947 in 1994, preliminary figures published by the Central Statistical Office (KSH) on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Housing construction has been boosted substantially by increased housing state subsidies at the end of 1994, KSH said.</p>
<p>But the number of permits for the construction of flats fell by 22 percent to 30,453 in 1996, which indicates that Hungarians already felt less encouraged for housing construction last year than in 1995, the KSH added.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
